    "notes": "PMTiles identifies the station footprint and track alignments. The long roof edge sets the heading. Nine entrance, eight surface rail and four elevated Métro sections stay clear in each tier. The station shows the heritage envelope, restored hall and above-ground transport arrangement. Construction equipment, temporary diversions, underground levels and future retail changes are outside the modeled scope. The 52-meter historic clear span follows SNCF documentation. Heights, façade recesses and the elevated Métro deck section are photo- and terrain-based reconstructions. The fitted hall floor and station-end railway grades follow the standard viewer terrain approaches. The modeled elevated Métro deck covers the station crossing and its immediate ends."
  },
